    "body": "How will we design multi-tenancy in the DMS? What terminology will we use to describe tenants / instances / etc? We may want to be more expansive and flexible in terms than in the ODS/API.\n\n[Azure: Fundamental Concepts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cloud-adoption-framework/ready/considerations/fundamental-concepts) may be a useful reference.\n\n----\n\nSaaS providers typically think of three multi-tenancy models for data storage:\n\n1. Complete database segregation.\n2. Segregation within a database, by schema\n3. Segregation within a table, by column\n\nMy own current thinking is that we probably want the flexibility of supporting two models. The schema approach is not as clean as the column approach, and we wouldn't pursue option 2.",
