     "created_at": "2025-03-12T17:28:55Z",
     "updated_at": "2025-03-12T17:28:55Z",
     "body": "Further considerations: \n\n1. Supporting two models increases the cost and complexity of maintenance and testing.\n2. Would multiple tenants end up streaming into the same distributed DB? (e.g. Kafka instance). Then we would need the tenant information in the stream, so that the data can be routed appropriately. Could possibly have separate topics (essentially the same as _schema_ segregation). Or, even if segregation by column is not used in the DMS authorization model, still might want to store the tenant ID in the database so that the value is available when reading the stream.",
     "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
